WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.290
USDC is a stablecoin, a digital token
designed to stay worth one US dollar.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.670
A business sends dollars to Circle.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.910
Circle creates matching USDC with equal value held in reserve.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:16.870
That's minting.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.350
Families usually buy tokens that already exist.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:25.170
When USDC moves between wallets, the reserve backing stays put.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.985
To redeem, an eligible customer returns USDC.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.570
Circle removes those tokens, called
burning, and sends dollars back.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.850
That backing and redemption help keep USDC near one dollar.
